{"project":"platform/upstream/llvm","branch":"tizen_base","id":"Ie2c1d45cea6703a0caef72187397275a03e66468","number":361624,"subject":"packaging: split tool subpackages into a standalone llvm-tools-subpkgs spec","owner":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"url":"https://review.tizen.org/gerrit/c/platform/upstream/llvm/+/361624","hashtags":[],"createdOn":1794638184,"lastUpdated":1795692188,"open":true,"status":"NEW","comments":[{"timestamp":1794638184,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 1."},{"timestamp":1794638257,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 1: Verified-1"},{"timestamp":1794638262,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Set Work In Progress"},{"timestamp":1795044644,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 2.\n\nOutdated Votes:\n* Verified-1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE\")\n"},{"timestamp":1795044663,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Set Ready For Review"},{"timestamp":1795044680,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 2: Verified+1"},{"timestamp":1795046250,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 3.\n\nOutdated Votes:\n* Verified+1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE\")\n"},{"timestamp":1795064791,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 3: Verified+1\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1795146544,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 4: Patch Set 3 was rebased\n\nOutdated Votes:\n* Verified+1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE\")\n"},{"timestamp":1795187618,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 5."},{"timestamp":1795188149,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Patch Set 5:\n\nPS5 on top of PS4: fixes for the in-tree BOLT build and the standalone llvm-tools-subpkgs spec. The PS4 history in the commit message is unchanged; a summary of the PS5 changes follows it.\n\nBOLT CMake\n- Add BOLT_LLVM_LINK_MODE, set before its consumers in bolt/CMakeLists.txt. It is empty only when BOLT is built standalone with LLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB\u003dON, and DISABLE_LLVM_LINK_LLVM_DYLIB otherwise. All BOLT libraries, tools and unit tests use it, so in-tree BOLT keeps linking the LLVM component libraries as before, and only the standalone dylib build links libLLVM.so.\n- X86BoltMnemonicTables.cpp is listed in LLVM_OPTIONAL_SOURCES and compiled only for standalone dylib builds; the mirror declarations are enabled under the same condition.\n- The inherited runtime C/C++ flags are cleared only for standalone builds; in-tree runtime flags are unchanged.\n- merge-fdata is installed once by CMake; the duplicate manual install is removed.\n\nllvm.spec\n- armv7l LLVM_TARGETS_TO_BUILD is back to ARM;BPF.\n- The explicit Requires: python3 on llvm is removed.\n\nllvm-tools-subpkgs.spec\n- ExclusiveArch: x86_64 aarch64, with BOLT_TARGETS_TO_BUILD set per architecture and a check that the expected targets are registered.\n- The LLVM provider BuildRequires (llvm, llvm-devel, llvm-static-devel, libllvm, libomp) are pinned to %{version}, and %build checks that the installed providers share one version and release.\n- bolt now requires libllvm \u003d %{version} at runtime (unversioned in PS4); its explicit Requires: compiler-rt is removed.\n- LLVM_LIBDIR_SUFFIX is derived from %{_lib} instead of a fixed 64.\n- The distribution $LDFLAGS are kept in the CMake linker flags, together with --build-id\u003dsha1.\n- The debug packaging comment now describes the actual flow (find-debuginfo via __debug_install_post, bolt-debuginfo and llvm-tools-subpkgs-debugsource).\n\nTested on x86_64: full llvm build with in-tree BOLT, and a standalone llvm-tools-subpkgs build against the installed llvm packages."},{"timestamp":1795188254,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Patch Set 5: Code-Review+1 Verified+1"},{"timestamp":1795584907,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 6.\n\nOutdated Votes:\n* Code-Review+1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE OR is:MIN\")\n* Verified+1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE\")\n"},{"timestamp":1795585235,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 5:\n\nReview of PS5 (no vote).\n\nBlocking-ish, addressed in PS6:\n1. packaging/llvm.spec: \"Obsoletes: clang-analyzer\" is on the llvm package, but the analyzer libexec scripts (ccc-analyzer, c++-analyzer, intercept-cc, ...) are owned by the clang package. The obsolete belongs on clang, and the comment \"llvm takes them over\" is inaccurate for those files.\n2. packaging/llvm.spec: analyze-build, intercept-build, scan-build and scan-build-py are in the llvm %files, but they run the libexec scripts that ship from clang. Installing llvm alone leaves them non-functional. clang already Requires llvm, so moving them to clang avoids the cycle the comment was trying to avoid.\n\nNon-blocking:\n3. llvm.spec %install comment says the openmp libgomp/libiomp5 symlinks land in $DESTDIR/usr/lib. The openmp install rule writes to $DESTDIR${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/${OPENMP_INSTALL_LIBDIR} (lib64 on 64-bit). The rm uses %{_libdir}, which matches that path, so only the comment is off.\n4. Commit message lists items that are already in the base (ARM;BPF target list, LLVM_LIBDIR_SUFFIX derivation, dropped python3 Requires) and not changes in this patchset. Worth rewording to describe what this change does.\n5. bolt/lib/Target/X86/X86GenSubSuperRegisterBody.inc and X86GenNeedsAddressSizeOverrideBody.inc match the upstream bodies in f346dd75 (ignoring whitespace). Minor: the #define macros in X86BoltMnemonicTables.cpp are not #undef\u0027d, and the is16BitMemOperand signature continuation is misaligned.\n\nNot verified: no gbs build. Before submit, please confirm on the built libLLVM.so.22.1 that X86::isNOP / getX86SubSuperRegister / needsAddressSizeOverride are not exported (nm -D --defined-only), otherwise the X86 mirror duplicates symbols."},{"timestamp":1795585235,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 6:\n\nReview of PS6 (no vote).\n\nAddresses items 1 and 2 from the PS5 review:\n- clang-analyzer Obsoletes moved from llvm to clang; the llvm comment is corrected.\n- analyze-build, intercept-build, scan-build and scan-build-py moved from the llvm %files to the clang %files. clang already Requires llvm, so there is no cycle.\n- llvm-tools-subpkgs.spec description updated to match the new ownership.\n\nVerified: the spec parses (rpmspec -q --srpm exits 0) and the diff has no whitespace errors. No gbs build yet.\n\nNon-blocking items 3-5 from the PS5 review are not addressed in this patchset."},{"timestamp":1795585395,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 6: Code-Review+1 Verified+1"},{"timestamp":1795604704,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 6:\n\nBuild verification for PS6 (no vote).\n\ngbs builds finished for x86_64, armv7l and aarch64 (aarch64 exit 0). RPM checks pass on all three:\n- analyze-build, intercept-build, scan-build and scan-build-py are owned by clang only\n- analyzer libexec scripts are in clang\n- llvm-xray, llvm-profgen and llvm-profdata are in llvm\n- Obsoletes placement is correct (clang-analyzer on clang; llvm-xray and llvm-prof-tools on llvm)\n- no llvm to clang requires cycle\n- bolt requires libllvm \u003d 22.1.8 with no compiler-rt (x86_64 and aarch64); bolt is absent on armv7l as expected\n\nNon-blocking items 3-5 are not addressed in this patchset. No further commits are planned for them."},{"timestamp":1795605349,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Patch Set 6:\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1795606722,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 6: Verified-1\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1795692188,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 7.\n\nOutdated Votes:\n* Code-Review+1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE OR is:MIN\")\n* Verified-1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE\")\n"}],"currentPatchSet":{"number":7,"revision":"de305f2c4de2721c7aeb5a677cd0ee32c3be505c","parents":["f346dd75e87de324dc2abe61454ca1c49969d12d"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/7","uploader":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"createdOn":1795692188,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"REWORK","sizeInsertions":690,"sizeDeletions":34},"patchSets":[{"number":1,"revision":"da885208aeb52f55c448ff46873d242346727522","parents":["61ef5d31ca91025c414c748477bef0c64ddfa67c"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/1","uploader":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"createdOn":1794638184,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Verified","description":"Verified","value":"-1","grantedOn":1794638257,"by":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"}}],"sizeInsertions":563,"sizeDeletions":30},{"number":2,"revision":"d1c32eb37fa1be1196923b839e405fd0d9de2955","parents":["61ef5d31ca91025c414c748477bef0c64ddfa67c"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/2","uploader":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"createdOn":1795044644,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Verified","description":"Verified","value":"1","grantedOn":1795044680,"by":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"}}],"sizeInsertions":574,"sizeDeletions":30},{"number":3,"revision":"420a8aab1106c307270a6730a0483c2adf23175c","parents":["7b05a13744d1cf81a5e9cff22a27eb037bf1b6a8"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/3","uploader":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"createdOn":1795046250,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Verified","description":"Verified","value":"1","grantedOn":1795064791,"by":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"}}],"comments":[{"file":"/PATCHSET_LEVEL","line":0,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"verified via https://quickbuild.tizen.org/build/1234572"}],"sizeInsertions":575,"sizeDeletions":30},{"number":4,"revision":"1ddecbe8729f832b5ef565092d039f68df647a43","parents":["f346dd75e87de324dc2abe61454ca1c49969d12d"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/4","uploader":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"createdOn":1795146544,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"TRIVIAL_REBASE","sizeInsertions":575,"sizeDeletions":30},{"number":5,"revision":"cbaa01f5c148f5cc705f969e13ac41fef811a9f9","parents":["f346dd75e87de324dc2abe61454ca1c49969d12d"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/5","uploader":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"createdOn":1795187618,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Verified","description":"Verified","value":"1","grantedOn":1795188254,"by":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"}},{"type":"Code-Review","description":"Code-Review","value":"1","grantedOn":1795188254,"by":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"}}],"sizeInsertions":650,"sizeDeletions":29},{"number":6,"revision":"06f3424c543a9645707f9afbbd9b5318280fffeb","parents":["f346dd75e87de324dc2abe61454ca1c49969d12d"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/6","uploader":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"createdOn":1795584907,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Code-Review","description":"Code-Review","value":"1","grantedOn":1795585395,"by":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"}},{"type":"Verified","description":"Verified","value":"-1","grantedOn":1795606722,"by":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"}}],"comments":[{"file":"/PATCHSET_LEVEL","line":0,"reviewer":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"message":"Hi~ Mr son\nThis is our review of PS6.\nThe analyzer moves in PS6 look correct to us.\n\nRe the open item from the PS5 review (exported X86 symbols): checked on the x86_64 build of this change (bolt/ is identical in PS5 and PS6). libLLVM.so.22.1 exports none of the functions defined by the BOLT X86 mirror (nm -D --defined-only), and the standalone llvm-bolt imports none of them from libLLVM (nm -D --undefined-only). The mirror definitions, including X86::isNOP, getX86SubSuperRegister and needsAddressSizeOverride, are local to llvm-bolt, so the mirror does not duplicate exported symbols.\n\nWhile checking the analyzer packaging we found a few more items. We are preparing fixes as small separate patches on top of PS6 and will post them here once they pass a full build:\n1. scan-build now ships in clang, but its report resources (/usr/share/scan-build/*) and its man page are in llvm-devel, which clang does not require, so scan-build installed with clang alone is missing the files it copies into its HTML report. The same applies to scan-view: the program is in llvm, its data is in llvm-devel. This is already the case in the base.\n2. analyze-build, intercept-build and scan-build-py import the libscanbuild and libear Python modules, which are not in any of the built RPMs. This is also already the case in the base.\n3. Add Provides: clang-analyzer, llvm-xray and llvm-prof-tools \u003d %{version}-%{release} next to the Obsoletes, with the Obsoletes bound changed to \"\u003c\" so that a package does not obsolete its own Provides. No package in the repositories we checked requires the old names, so this is hygiene rather than a breakage fix.\n4. Your non-blocking items 3 (OpenMP symlink comment) and 5 (#undef and alignment in X86BoltMnemonicTables.cpp).\n5. Commit message body: rewritten to describe the change against the base, as you noted in item 4.\n\nCould you hold the submit until these are posted? If you prefer to merge PS6 first, we can send them as a follow-up change instead."},{"file":"/PATCHSET_LEVEL","line":0,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Sure~ Thanks for checking the X86 symbols on the build. We\u0027ll wait to submit until the fix patches are posted and reviewed on top of PS6."}],"sizeInsertions":650,"sizeDeletions":32},{"number":7,"revision":"de305f2c4de2721c7aeb5a677cd0ee32c3be505c","parents":["f346dd75e87de324dc2abe61454ca1c49969d12d"],"ref":"refs/changes/24/361624/7","uploader":{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},"createdOn":1795692188,"author":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"kind":"REWORK","sizeInsertions":690,"sizeDeletions":34}],"submitRecords":[{"status":"NOT_READY","labels":[{"label":"Verified","status":"NEED"},{"label":"Code-Review","status":"NEED"}]}],"allReviewers":[{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},{"name":"Lin Hao","email":"hao.lin@samsung.com","username":"lhmax2025"},{"name":"fangyu fangyu.he","email":"fangyu.he@samsung.com","username":"fangyu.he"},{"name":"Liu Shanshan","email":"ss0217.liu@samsung.com","username":"liushanshan"},{"name":"Juitem JoonWoo Kim","email":"jw1772.kim@samsung.com","username":"juitem"},{"name":"Pareek Eshaan","email":"e.pareek@samsung.com","username":"eshaanpareek"}]}
